    {
      "name": "set_code_cell_value",
      "description": "Set a code cell that will be evaluated by Quadratic. Supported languages: Python, Javascript.\n\nCRITICAL Python rules:\n- The LAST LINE of the cell is the return value (an expression, not a statement). Do NOT use the `return` keyword.\n- Only ONE output per cell: one value, one DataFrame, OR one chart. Use separate code cells for multiple outputs.\n- Reference spreadsheet data with q.cells(): q.cells('A1'), q.cells('A1:C7'), q.cells('Table1'), q.cells(\"Table1[column]\")\n- Use first_row_header=True when referencing ranges with headers: q.cells('A1:B9', first_row_header=True)\n- Charts: ONLY Plotly is supported. Use fig.show() to display. Do NOT use matplotlib, seaborn .plot(), df.hist(), or any Pandas plotting.\n- Default packages: pandas, numpy, scipy, plotly, scikit-learn, statsmodels, nltk, regex, requests\n- Install additional packages with: import micropip; await micropip.install(\"package_name\")\n- Do NOT use: try-except, conditional returns, print() for output, return keyword, from js import document, Polars, file I/O functions\n- Each code cell is isolated — imports and variables must be defined in every cell that uses them.\n- For trendlines in Plotly, you MUST import statsmodels.\n- Cross-sheet references: q.cells(\"'Sheet_name'!A1:C9\")\n- Tables are global (no sheet prefix): q.cells(\"Table1\")",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "sheet_name": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ],
            "description": "Sheet name"
          },
          "code_cell_name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Name for the output of the code cell (no spaces or special chars, _ allowed)"
          },
          "code_cell_language": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "Python",
              "Javascript"
            ],
            "description": "The language of the code cell"
          },
          "code_cell_position": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Cell position in A1 notation, e.g. \"A1\""
          },
          "code_string": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The code to run in the cell"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "code_cell_name",
          "code_cell_language",
          "code_cell_position",
          "code_string"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      }
    },
